. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5c7433c4c7c8fc02\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7eb4d848fd7ece4d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7eb4d848fd7ece4d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc917bac22ce3b9b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Grade 8 Mathematics · State Score Change Summary · Average Scale Scores: 2019-2022 · US map. Data are provided in the table below. Between 2019 and 2022 · 0 · states/jurisdictions · had a score increase · 2 · states/jurisdictions · had no significant change in score · 51 · states/jurisdictions · had a score decrease · + National · Public · DoDEA · Alabama · Kentucky · North Dakota · Utah · Alaska · Arizona ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc917bac22ce3b9b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"48c1e7ef87adeecc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"48c1e7ef87adeecc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee5352de356f4e4a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 3