{"type": "message", "id": "7d0812db", "parentId": "ce92ee6b", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:28:48.403Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool-1ffd3c1310974c83bcb5689eff774b73", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Kentucky score 270 280\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 908,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d12149e2cbb7d7ec\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d12149e2cbb7d7ec\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35ff933d1a1df587\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35ff933d1a1df587\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"41d9448591b26f7c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"41d9448591b26f7c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"10042ced805c5f21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"10042ced805c5f21\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"386d00cdb47ff37a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"386d00cdb47ff37a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b33b048d1ccb3f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics score decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2003. In 2022, fourth- and eighth-grade mathematics scores declined for most states/jurisdictions as well as for most participating urban districts compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from 0 to 500.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b33b048d1ccb3f8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7717580076e1a6a3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7717580076e1a6a3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c1a7cbac2b3a4b9b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c1a7cbac2b3a4b9b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5c0bf397fbb97c40\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5c0bf397fbb97c40\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c3dc0d257d47e89\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c3dc0d257d47e89\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Kentucky score 270 280", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 908, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d12149e2cbb7d7ec\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d12149e2cbb7d7ec\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35ff933d1a1df587\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35ff933d1a1df587\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"41d9448591b26f7c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"41d9448591b26f7c\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"10042ced805c5f21\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"10042ced805c5f21\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"386d00cdb47ff37a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"386d00cdb47ff37a\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2b33b048d1ccb3f8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics score decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2003. In 2022, fourth- and eighth-grade mathematics scores declined for most states/jurisdictions as well as for most participating urban districts compared to 2019. Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from 0 to 500.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2b33b048d1ccb3f8\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7717580076e1a6a3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7717580076e1a6a3\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c1a7cbac2b3a4b9b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c1a7cbac2b3a4b9b\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5c0bf397fbb97c40\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5c0bf397fbb97c40\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6c3dc0d257d47e89\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6c3dc0d257d47e89\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775302128402}}
